# Fingerprints of real credentials that were revoked or rotated at their
# provider. History is not rewritten, so a rotated secret stays in old
# commits. Its fingerprint here records that it was handled.
#
# Format (one per line): <commit>:<file>:<rule-id>:<line> for `gitleaks git`
# findings, or <file>:<rule-id>:<line> for `gitleaks dir` findings.
# Generate entries from a gitleaks JSON report (the `Fingerprint` field),
# never by hand, and record the rotation in
# docs/security/open-source-release-audit.md.
#
# The pre-release audit found no real credentials, so this file has no entries.
